course: dictionary
lesson: 7113
title: One word, two jobs: pedal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pedal can be a noun or a verb, so the job the word does in the sentence tells you its meaning. As a noun, a pedal is a part you push with your foot. As a verb, to pedal means to push those parts round to make a bike go.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Going up the steep hill to school, you click to a bigger back cog: you pedal more turns, but each turn is easy.» Here pedal is a verb, because you are doing something to make the bike move.
explain: Now look at «the brake pedal». Pedal is a noun here, the part you press with your foot. Brake tells you what it is for, because a brake is what slows a car down.
explain: A good check is to swap in your meaning. If «pedal more turns» still makes sense as «push the pedals more turns», then your verb meaning is right.
fact: Pedal (noun) means a part you push with your foot to make a bike move, or to control a machine, car or piano.
fact: Pedal (verb) means to push the pedals of a bike to make it go.
fact: «Pedal hard» means push the pedals with a lot of force.
fact: «Brake pedal» is the pedal in a car that you press to slow it down.
fact: Gears are toothed wheels; «a low gear» makes pedalling easier on a hill, and «a high gear» is good for going fast on the flat.
exercise: «Going up the steep hill to school, you click to a bigger back cog: you pedal more turns, but each turn is easy.» What is pedal in this sentence? | A noun: a bin you open with your foot | *A verb: to push the pedals to make the bike go | A noun: a part of a car you press to stop | A verb: to stop suddenly
exercise: Lily says pedal is only a bike word. What does pedal mean in «She pressed the piano pedal»? | To pedal a bike backwards | A small bell on a bike | *A part you press with your foot to control a piano | A part of a bike you wear on your head
exercise: «A low gear turns the wheel less for each turn of the pedals, so you push more gently but pedal more times up a hill.» Which gear helps you climb a hill? | The helmet | A high gear | *A low gear | The chain
test: In «Wear a helmet and pedal steadily», what does pedal mean? | *To push the pedals of a bike to make it go | A part of a car that holds the wheel | To wear a helmet | A bin you open with your foot
test: Which phrase names the pedal you press to slow a car? | pedal hard | *brake pedal | pedal bin | piano pedal
exam: Ben reads «The gears on a bike are toothed wheels joined by the chain: a big one makes pedalling easier.» Which is true? | The chain is a kind of pedal | *A big gear makes pedalling easier | A small gear makes pedalling easier | Gears are not used on bikes
